<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="defending-and-discipline" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip files-touched rows and callouts follow the sibling plan fragments' inline markup so the page renders them identically -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/team.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The acting keeper is derived from the team's state: slot 0 while it plays, else a goalkeeper who came on, else the most advanced outfield player. A lone survivor keeps its place across the pitch. The back line is never wider than one tuned gap per space between its players, so it narrows as players leave. One fewer player presses for each player out of play.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>team</td><td>+120 / -20</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/decision.rs, sim.rs, player.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Pressers run at the point where they can meet the carrier. One back-line defender covers the most advanced central attacker, goal-side. Every keeper check uses the acting keeper. A tackler in its foul cooldown makes no tackle attempt, and a booked player fouls less.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>play</td><td>+144 / -33</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/rules/*</summary><div class="pl-card">Every foul starts the tackler's cooldown, advantage included. A player holds at most one card per advantage spell, the most severe, and is never shown two cards on one tick. Penalties, the shoot-out and restarts use the acting keeper, and a restart reads the team's own end from its attack direction, not from a parked keeper.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>rules</td><td>+106 / -28</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/ai.rs, tactics/change.rs, commentary</summary><div class="pl-card">After a keeper's red card, the computer manager brings on its bench keeper for the acting keeper when a substitution is left (decision sub-keeper, with three commentary lines). Every substitution lays the team out again.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>ai</td><td>+48 / -3</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">infrastructure</span> crates/engine/src/tuning.rs, snapshot.rs, scenario.rs; content/tuning.json</summary><div class="pl-card">Five bounded tuning values with defaults (cover distance, cover channel, back-line gap, foul cooldown, booked factor); an older tuning file still loads. The snapshot moves to version 5 to carry each player's foul cooldown.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>state</td><td>+58 / -4</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/defending.rs, discipline.rs, acting_keeper.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A regression scene for each mechanism, and three slow criterion runs: the sending-off experiment over 120 seeds, every shipped formation against 4-4-2 over 120 seeds, and discipline over 200 matches.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>engine-tests</td><td>+630</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests (rules, commentary, snapshot, content)</summary><div class="pl-card">Updated calls and re-derived expectations, each recorded with its value before and after.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>engine-tests</td><td>+31 / -8</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> docs/reference/data-files.md, protocol.md; content/commentary/en.json</summary><div class="pl-card">The five tuning rows, the foul paragraph, and the sub-keeper decision value and its lines.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>docs</td><td>+25 / -2</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Formations far outside the limit today (high).</strong> Seven of nine pairings against 4-4-2 have a side above 4.0 goals per match; 4-4-1-1 averages 11.60. If the three defending mechanisms cannot fix a pairing inside their bounds, implement stops and reports it.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Every seeded result moves (medium).</strong> Pinned tests are re-derived and recorded with values before and after, never loosened.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Goals fall below the band (medium).</strong> Card chaos made about 23 percent of goals. The misses are recorded against the baseline; realism-tuning retunes.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Per-tick cost (medium).</strong> The cover search and the intercept solve run every tick. The gate is 1.6228 microseconds per tick.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Validator drift rule (low).</strong> Cover applies only while the opponents hold the ball in the defending half, so the anchor rule keeps reading zero violations.</aside>
  </div>
  <style>
    .fragment-plan .pl-files { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files th, .fragment-plan .pl-files td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); vertical-align: top; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-files summary { cursor: pointer; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-chip { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid currentColor; margin-right: 6px; opacity: 0.8; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-card { padding: 6px 0 4px 18px; opacity: 0.9; }
    .fragment-plan .pl-risks { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .fragment-plan .pl-files th:nth-child(3), .fragment-plan .pl-files td:nth-child(3) { display: none; } }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-plan');
      var files = 26, modules = 8;
      var risks = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.pl-risks .callout').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'plan', artifact: 'plan', counts: { files: files, modules: modules, risks: risks } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
